# Hual04a route (item86 re-time on the integrated engine-fidelity tree): six kills, earned
# card, bureau card-reader, bureau fuse and the Cine1 LastWave fight.
#
# The automatic AI bursts (`Pawn.PressingFire` reads the controller bFire byte) tripled the
# incoming damage, so the route fights each soldier from before it closes, crouches under the
# charged soldier's burst and heals on the base medkit. The base medkit fight tracks the head
# band (0.90) so BaseSoldier4 dies before its burst drains the route, preserving health for the
# bureau leg. The route then reads the earned card at MagneticPassTrigger4, walks to the bureau
# fuse (`Hual04aFusiblePick0`, event `FusibleRamasse`) and kills the `Cine1` `LastWave`
# reinforcement (tabActions[35] `Event LastWave01 LastWave03 LastWave04` spawns
# BaseSoldier/BaseSoldier2/BaseSoldier3) by input, so goal 2 (find the fuse) completes.
#
# The route then, after the LastWave, walks back through the base to the bureau
# circuit-breaker: `use Porte21` opens the electrical-box door, `track XIIIGoalTrigger19` aims
# at the exposed fuse socket so the game's own `ReturnTrace` targets the trigger, and the
# carried fuse's `EventItem.UseMe` completes goal 3 (install the fuse). `use XIIIMover1` works
# the cable-car lever; its `FinishedOpening` fires `ManetteTele` -> `SetGoalComplete(94)`, which
# completes goal 4 (activate the cable-car) and fires the map's `TeleOn`. `item90` implemented
# Core.dll `execArrayElement`'s out-of-range fixed-array clamp, so `Hual04a.SetGoalComplete`
# case 3's `i < 4` over the 3-entry `SoldiersEnRenforts` array no longer errors.
#
# item94 (goal 5, `Rejoin Carrington in front of the cable-car cabin`): after the lever the
# route walks back through `Porte12` and around the station's north side down to the boarding
# platform below the station floor (`PositionInfo23`, 945.8,393.8,-105), following the path a
# collision-world BFS of the real walker finds (the direct line south is walled). The post-lever
# cine's `tp 23` (`CineController2.TeleportTo` -> `Actor.SetLocation`) is then refused by the VM
# world-placement check, so Carrington never reaches the platform and the cine stays parked at
# `wait player 128`; goal 5 and the Hual04c travel remain unclaimed (pinned, see the report).
#
# Input only: no teleport, set_goal, take_control, extra weapon grant or health edit. The
# Beretta grant at t=0.5 is the carried-loadout diagnostic (see hual02_route.script).
# Coordinates and times are Unreal units/seconds. The integrated volume-brush overlap fires
# DetectionVolume4/5 (`Degage`/`dernierpoint`) and starts `Cine1.Play(2)`.
t=0.50 weapon xiii.Beretta
t=1.00 switch_weapon 2
t=2.50 goto -10200 -1500
t=6.00 goto -9600 -1600
t=10.00 goto -9042 -2286
t=14.00 goto -8582 -2333
t=18.00 goto -8058 -2049
t=22.00 goto -7433 -1524
t=26.00 goto -6741 -1012
t=30.00 goto -6432 320
t=34.00 goto -6172 -533
t=38.00 goto -5625 4
t=42.00 goto -5522 462
t=46.00 goto -5105 1301
t=50.00 goto -4474 2524
t=54.00 goto -3645 1693
t=58.00 goto -3302 1388
t=62.00 goto -3203 1209
t=66.00 goto -3140 300
t=70.00 goto -3160 -600
# item107: closed-loop fights. `engage` turns to the visible hostile, holds the fire button (an
# automatic weapon refires at its own rate, the Beretta is re-pressed, an empty weapon is
# reloaded or swapped for a carried one) and ends once nothing has been visible for a second, so
# a change in when the soldiers close in no longer breaks the route; `loot` walks onto the
# visible corpses that still carry a weapon (the game hands the weapon over on contact).
# The rifleman BaseSoldier1 is fought first from the (-3160,-600) stop, before the burst fire
# ramps up: its M16 and ammo are what the rest of the canyon and the base fights need.
t=72.00 engage BaseSoldier1 3000 20
t=72.00 loot 2500 20
t=72.10 switch_weapon 11
t=72.20 reload
# The shotgun soldier (BaseSoldier5) and the alerted third canyon soldier (BaseSoldier0) are
# killed from a crouch; with the ledge rule (item101) BaseSoldier0 holds at (-2720,-1177) in
# `Attaque` and shoots the route, so the stand needs a longer burst. Then both corpses are
# walked over for the dropped M16s + ammo the base fights need.
t=72.30 crouch 1
t=72.40 engage 3000 40
t=72.50 crouch 0
t=72.60 loot 3000 30
t=72.80 reload
t=101.80 goto -2400 -1600
t=105.80 goto -1800 -1400
t=108.80 goto -1400 -1300
t=122.80 goto -1899 -1821
t=126.80 goto -1280 -900
t=129.30 goto -1280 -272
